WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:16.688
school I opened my backpack to show Molly the bell for Caswell.

2
00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:19.169
But the bell was gone!

3
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.392
Before I could tell Molly about it, Mrs.

4
00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:24.633
Romano made a surprise announcement.

5
00:00:24.653 --> 00:00:28.256
"Class, I have something exciting to share!"

6
00:00:29.368 --> 00:00:31.490
"Are we going to have an ice cream party?"

7
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:32.751
asked Colby.

8
00:00:32.771 --> 00:00:35.314
"Or take a trip to the zoo?"

9
00:00:35.754 --> 00:00:36.435
said Ruby.

10
00:00:36.455 --> 00:00:39.277
"Maybe we're getting a class pet.

11
00:00:39.618 --> 00:00:40.879
I'd like a monkey!"

12
00:00:41.319 --> 00:00:42.140
said Kristin.

13
00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:44.422
Mrs. Romano smiled.

14
00:00:44.442 --> 00:00:46.864
"No, we're not getting a monkey.

15
00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:51.488
There's going to be an Invention Convention in our own city!"

16
00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:52.549
she said.

17
00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:55.072
I sat up straighter in my chair.

18
00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.481
"An Invention Convention will be held one week from today," Mrs.

19
00:01:00.521 --> 00:01:01.361
Romano said.

20
00:01:01.381 --> 00:01:07.403
"Students can exhibit their inventions, and there will be prizes for the best ones."

21
00:01:07.423 --> 00:01:09.904
"An Invention Convention?"

22
00:01:10.184 --> 00:01:12.444
I thought, forgetting about my bell problem.

23
00:01:12.464 --> 00:01:16.546
"Wow!" Molly raised her hand.

24
00:01:16.566 --> 00:01:19.766
"What do you get for first prize, Mrs.

25
00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:26.088
Romano?" "First prize is a blue ribbon and one hundred dollars!"

26
00:01:26.129 --> 00:01:26.789
our teacher told us.

27
00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.612
I let out a low whistle.

28
00:01:30.693 --> 00:01:31.934
One hundred dollars!

29
00:01:33.275 --> 00:01:35.397
I wondered if that was enough to help my mom.

30
00:01:36.298 --> 00:01:39.440
Then I started thinking about the magic thinking box again.

31
00:01:40.361 --> 00:01:43.304
That was an even better invention than Caswell's bell.

32
00:01:44.605 --> 00:01:47.988
If I could make a box that worked, I might win a prize.

33
00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:52.352
And then I could figure out what my mom was so worried about!

34
00:01:54.048 --> 00:01:58.511
That afternoon Josh, Jenny, Molly, and I walked home from school together.

35
00:01:58.531 --> 00:02:02.034
"Did your teacher tell you about the Invention Convention?"

36
00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:03.255
I asked Josh.

37
00:02:03.275 --> 00:02:05.876
"Yes," said Josh.

38
00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:09.539
"I'd like to invent an automatic homework machine."

39
00:02:09.559 --> 00:02:13.402
"We'd never have to do homework again!"

40
00:02:14.062 --> 00:02:14.723
said Jenny.

41
00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:17.184
Molly was chewing bubble gum.

42
00:02:17.204 --> 00:02:23.921
"I'd like to invent gum that doesn't lose its flavor," she said, popping a big bubble.

43
00:02:23.941 --> 00:02:28.844
"Iggy, you could build your magic thinking box for the convention!"

44
00:02:29.325 --> 00:02:30.045
said Josh.

45
00:02:30.065 --> 00:02:32.847
"You just read my mind!"

46
00:02:33.247 --> 00:02:33.848
I told him.

47
00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:37.810
"What's a magic thinking box?"

48
00:02:38.371 --> 00:02:39.131
asked Molly.

49
00:02:39.151 --> 00:02:42.273
"It's a special box," I explained.

50
00:02:42.293 --> 00:02:46.296
"You put it on your head, and then I can tell what you're thinking."

51
00:02:47.237 --> 00:02:48.337
Molly looked puzzled.

52
00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:50.359
"But how does it work?"

53
00:02:51.259 --> 00:02:52.120
she wanted to know.

54
00:02:53.508 --> 00:02:56.250
I was glad we had reached our apartment building by then.

55
00:02:57.211 --> 00:03:00.013
Because I didn't have an answer for Molly's question.

56
00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:05.336
The truth is, I had no idea how my magic thinking box would work.

57
00:03:06.337 --> 00:03:08.098
I just hoped it would work.

58
00:03:09.679 --> 00:03:11.821
Upstairs, my mom was on the phone again.

59
00:03:11.841 --> 00:03:16.444
"Well, I just don't have enough money," she said.

60
00:03:16.464 --> 00:03:18.745
I couldn't believe it.

61
00:03:19.706 --> 00:03:21.867
She was talking about money again too!

62
00:03:23.688 --> 00:03:26.690
I went into my room and threw my backpack on the floor.

63
00:03:28.131 --> 00:03:29.491
Tate was doing his homework.

64
00:03:30.352 --> 00:03:31.612
"Move that backpack!"

65
00:03:32.073 --> 00:03:32.673
he yelled.

66
00:03:32.693 --> 00:03:35.394
"It's on my side of the room again!"

67
00:03:35.414 --> 00:03:37.796
"Just barely!"

68
00:03:38.196 --> 00:03:39.176
I argued back.

69
00:03:39.197 --> 00:03:41.658
"Boys, please!"

70
00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:43.079
my mother called.

71
00:03:43.099 --> 00:03:45.240
"I'm on the telephone."

72
00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.942
I kicked my backpack under my bed.

73
00:03:49.922 --> 00:03:52.644
At least Tate couldn't say that was on his side of the room.

74
00:03:54.924 --> 00:03:56.585
Then I flopped onto my bed.

75
00:03:56.605 --> 00:04:00.226
I needed to think about my magic thinking box.

76
00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.168
How would it work, anyway?

77
00:04:04.148 --> 00:04:07.970
I wanted to win a prize at the Invention Convention more than anything.

78
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.191
I also wanted to find out what was bothering my mom.

79
00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.833
But how was I going to make a magic thinking box?

80
00:04:16.933 --> 00:04:18.814
I'd need real magic for that.

81
00:04:20.135 --> 00:04:21.235
I remembered Mr.

82
00:04:21.335 --> 00:04:22.876
Chen's one-way mirror.

83
00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.345
You could see through it on one side, Josh had said.

84
00:04:28.286 --> 00:04:31.530
But on the other side, it was just like a regular mirror.

85
00:04:32.892 --> 00:04:38.239
Maybe a one-way mirror was exactly what I needed for my new invention!
